# Caddy on the Pi: the only process listening on the network.
#
# Each app is named explicitly rather than covered by a wildcard, so the certificates on
# this box are scoped to exactly these hostnames and nothing else on the domain.
#
# Certificates come over DNS-01, because nothing here is reachable from the internet and
# the usual HTTP challenge needs a public address on port 80. Caddy renews them itself.
# The token lives in /etc/caddy/cloudflare.env, root-readable only, scoped to Zone -> DNS
# -> Edit on this one zone.
#
# Both A records point at the Pi's private address (192.168.68.69) and must be "DNS only"
# in Cloudflare. A proxied record cannot point at a private address.

(house) {
	tls {
		dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}
		# Ask public resolvers for the challenge record rather than whatever the Pi's
		# DHCP handed it, which may be the router answering for the local zone.
		resolvers 1.1.1.1 8.8.8.8
	}
}

recipes.julianjelfs.co.uk {
	import house
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8010
}

